From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 16:57:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: gpu: img,powervr-rogue: Add an OPP table and a
 supply

The GPU of the Allwinner A733 needs its core supply at 960 mV before
its clock runs at 1008 MHz. The board sets that voltage when the PMIC
probes and the clock when the GPU probes, and nothing in the device
tree orders the two. An operating point makes the pair a property of
the node: the OPP core raises the voltage before it raises the clock.

Add operating-points-v2 and gpu-supply, both optional, and require the
table when a supply is given, as the supply is used with it only. The
name follows the Mali bindings, which name the supply after the GPU
(mali-supply). A generic name such as power-supply would also match
chargers and batteries; this binding names no GPU rail
so far.

The properties are not limited to one compatible: the driver reads them
from the node and ignores a node without them, so the other users of the
binding keep their behaviour.

Not covered: a dt_binding_check run, dt-schema was not available.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards with the GPU node
carrying an OPP table and gpu-supply; the driver binds, takes the supply
and sets the operating point.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../bindings/gpu/img,powervr-rogue.yaml           | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpu/img,powervr-rogue.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpu/img,powervr-rogue.yaml
index 3c658926300c..fedbd189a94c 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpu/img,powervr-rogue.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpu/img,powervr-rogue.yaml
@@ -73,6 +73,18 @@ properties:
   interrupts:
     maxItems: 1
 
+  gpu-supply:
+    description:
+      Regulator that supplies the GPU core, used together with
+      operating-points-v2; the OPP core sets its voltage before it raises
+      the core clock.
+
+  operating-points-v2:
+    description:
+      Operating points of the GPU core clock. The driver sets the highest
+      one once at probe, before the firmware reads the clock rate, and
+      does not change it afterwards.
+
   power-domains:
     minItems: 1
     maxItems: 2
@@ -95,6 +107,9 @@ required:
   - clock-names
   - interrupts
 
+dependencies:
+  gpu-supply: [ operating-points-v2 ]
+
 additionalProperties: false
 
 allOf:
